    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0264" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg184"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1672.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that permission
                    has been granted the United States ship <hi rendition="#italic">Enterprise</hi>
                    (Massachusetts nautical school ship) to pass through the Kaiser Wilhelm (Kiel)
                    Canal, en route to the North Sea, in accordance with a request made by the
                    embassy a few days ago. This request was made at the instance of Commander
                    Edward M. Hughes, United States Navy, commanding the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Enterprise</hi>, who is at present cruising in the Baltic Sea and expects
                    to arrive at Kiel about August 1.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Andrew D. White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
